# Command: Implement a New Routing Strategy

Follow this checklist to add a new routing strategy to Hyperswitch.

## Step 1: Implement the strategy module

Create `crates/router/src/core/payments/<strategy_name>.rs`:

```rust
use api_models::routing::RoutableConnectorChoice;
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
use crate::logger;

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Default, Deserialize, Serialize)]
pub struct MyStrategyConfig { /* fields */ }

pub struct MyStrategy<'a> {
    config: &'a MyStrategyConfig,
}

impl<'a> MyStrategy<'a> {
    pub fn new(config: &'a MyStrategyConfig) -> Self { Self { config } }

    /// `now_param` — inject non-deterministic inputs for testability.
    pub fn apply(
        &self,
        connectors: Vec<RoutableConnectorChoice>,
        payment_id: &str,
        now_param: /* type */,
    ) -> Vec<RoutableConnectorChoice> {
        // pure transformation + logger::info! for observability
    }
}
```

## Step 2: Register the module

In `crates/router/src/core/payments.rs`:
```rust
pub mod my_strategy_name;
```

## Step 3: Add config to Settings

In `crates/router/src/configs/settings.rs`, inside `Settings<S>`:
```rust
#[serde(default)]
pub my_strategy: crate::core::payments::my_strategy_name::MyStrategyConfig,
```

## Step 4: Integrate in routing

